Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted]

scrapli/ffi.py:_get_zig_style_arch() is the runtime counterpart of setup.py's
build-time arch detection: it names the bundled libscrapli shared object file
to dlopen at import time. It raises LibScrapliException for any arch other
than x86_64/aarch64, so without this, scrapli cannot load its native library
on riscv64 even once a riscv64 wheel exists.

diff --git a/scrapli/ffi.py b/scrapli/ffi.py
index f76af6e..3f9ce47 100644
--- a/scrapli/ffi.py
+++ b/scrapli/ffi.py
@@ -49,6 +49,9 @@ def _get_zig_style_arch() -> str:
     if p in {"arm64", "aarch64"}:
         return "aarch64"
 
+    if p in {"riscv64"}:
+        return "riscv64"
+
     raise LibScrapliException(f"unsupported arch '{p}'")
 
 
